{"title":"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Official_MAA_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Official MAA 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Official_MAA_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Official MAA 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(similar_ideas_to_Solution_1,_but_faster)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (similar ideas to Solution 1, but faster)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2d7ea565d37a232bf9b8c0dbc0958e4a1924a35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^3+2^3+3^3+\\cdots +n^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"16\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/6134d694f7081592c60bbcca0f685a92b33af110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />, the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The formula for the sum of cubes, also known as Nicomachus's Theorem, is as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4d92ef4249f563e14028784c9ef0f239981863.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1^3+2^3+3^3+\\dots+k^3=(1+2+3+\\dots+k)^2=\\left(\\frac{k(k+1)}{2}\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"495\" height=\"46\" />\nfor any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>So let's apply this to this problem.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95a4743e64a2926abd095a04d00d693a8def6dc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=n+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />. Then we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/483a75895cb1cb143d9794ddd9f5fc879cf9a6c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 1^3+2^3+3^3+\\dots+(m-5)^3&amp;\\equiv 17 \\mod m \\\\ \\left(\\frac{(m-5)(m-4)}{2}\\right)^2&amp;\\equiv 17 \\mod m \\\\ \\left(\\dfrac{m(m-9)+20}2\\right)^2&amp;\\equiv 17\\mod m \\\\ \\left(m(m-9)+20\\right)^2&amp;\\equiv 4\\cdot 17\\mod m \\\\ \\left(20\\right)^2&amp;\\equiv 68\\mod m \\\\ 332 &amp;\\equiv 0 \\mod m \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"366\" height=\"205\" />\nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/2/8621e5d8e23fed01f82027ac2df840bc66d5b25b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\in\\{83,166,332\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />. Testing the cases, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d7950a6311d26bb487f53665422afeba8c3c47a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$332$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> fails. This leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53fdd3f58a748718e92396bf93bf4d306b11e77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78+161=\\boxed{239}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/latex.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\LaTeX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> and formatting adjustments and intermediate steps for clarification by Technodoggo.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Official_MAA_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Official_MAA_1)\">Solution 2 (Official MAA 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Official MAA 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the cubes from 1 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae6a2525964d90a7890e234c80b4209e52702782.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1^3+2^3+\\cdots+n^3=\\frac{n^2(n+1)^2}{4}.\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"39\" />For this to be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f84ecbb128ad520fef1ac8b7c607af6a4dddbd1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+5)q+17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, it must be that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e169704db9dab5472ef630fa00e1c3a06df7e4f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2(n+1)^2=4(n+5)q+4\\cdot 17,\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"19\" />so<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac0f6caa010b5b23966293f393f749eda4674c55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2(n+1)^2 \\equiv 4 \\cdot 17= 68\\hskip-.2cm \\pmod{n+5}.\\]\" width=\"298\" height=\"20\" />But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/097269954f5f210a7f5503e1996f12f621518b8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2(n+1)^2 \\equiv (-5)^2(-4)^2 = 400 \\pmod{n+5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"356\" height=\"19\" /> Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/6/7c66ac0c1c620e01ee59ccd2535644a321858f24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2(n+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" /> is congruent to both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/9782dd7447f84ce6adcf7945b86038e379c618f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$68$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b9f441cb219b6cfd9c19f7ae3ffc34506894cd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> which implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/6134d694f7081592c60bbcca0f685a92b33af110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15ed757d1bc4cf63a4a02206fe55199b7bff45d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400-68 = 332=2^2 \\cdot 83$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"190\" height=\"15\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b5832f62e45425928a84c0814d383f0b30573e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+5 &gt; 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />, the only choices for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/6134d694f7081592c60bbcca0f685a92b33af110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/edd6f474f8e81b85cb85a387b8a01a980f014a90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$83, 166,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2664cd3e2912c4259310ecdaabe77f4fcfc08e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$332.$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> Checking all three cases verifies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/583d4ace70eecd93c218633698b4d58c3486afcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=78$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/daf2ec251ca13e8fc39012d2c932e2d49af95728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=161$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> work, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/958df7f4550dab0cbf5f653a352cbd9f1b4485b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=327$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" /> does not. The requested sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec2ffc04df49ecba661b511244ed4bf3d0a1c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78+161 = 239$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Official_MAA_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Official_MAA_2)\">Solution 3 (Official MAA 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Official MAA 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the cubes of the integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e13775578697915561387b49dc50bae261740d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1^3+2^3+\\cdots+n^3=\\frac{n^2(n+1)^2}{4},\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"39\" />which, when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/6134d694f7081592c60bbcca0f685a92b33af110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />, has quotient<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5baeabfbf43edb43adb1dce94736959b9fb6861.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q=\\frac14n^3 -\\frac34n^2+4n-20 = \\frac{n^2(n-3)}4+4n-20\\]\" width=\"390\" height=\"39\" />with remainder <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/5121aafc33f20a7ad4df93a0f7bc7b63077a5bc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2659fe9ff33c527f54d2ad69e9ba6dd084a3d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pmod4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is an integer, and<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9dad73b5cb36949709db460a11fbbcab8b1b7d16.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n^2(n+1)^2}{4} = (n+5)Q + 100 \\equiv 17\\pmod{n+5},\\]\" width=\"390\" height=\"39\" />so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/6134d694f7081592c60bbcca0f685a92b33af110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/3120679d2663bd0e9bbae5d568451067299f87ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 - 17 =83$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f38dec72a31e27e582eceab61333529c2c4cc3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 78$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/49113a5774326f02aafa54dd6e1a30e49cacf238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 1 \\pmod4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is half of an integer, and letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b669a4aef879d5fd1ba87b7ec11649fc63b269ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> gives<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/2/a82038d56872012207e80bc51862d0e2abc5cde8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n^2(n+1)^2}{4} = 2(2k+3)Q + 100 \\equiv 17\\pmod{n+5}.\\]\" width=\"407\" height=\"39\" />Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/599d2c8baf99c8703253d7ccd03e2842d87ec64c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/1105321811665095e3b1f6db1d707ce4c304f563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100-17 = 83$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/90755691daeeb757dee46189e0cb45bded3324b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96294f38cb4557f55aa7fee142a34ea86b2a018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 161$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. The requested sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cfeb0a7b5f24d9e18bdf21868795a7f4d71bc85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$161 + 78 = 239$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the formula for  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c0e23ccbbb6675a0e3d3c78c42d87936192673.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^n  k^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"44\" height=\"48\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c33c7d80b3603e192a1c79b2acce64853a3b40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + ... + n^3 = \\frac{n^2(n+1)^2}{4}\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"39\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/03054437cf44f01105fd43ab78c86d80c8079dc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + ... + n^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"170\" height=\"16\" /> divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/d/7dd8b1b9017014c56c0f273336fc1b959169e1cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84830d1d6c5b19421f990b51396e90346107885.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n^2(n+1)^2}{4} \\equiv 17\\pmod {n + 5}\\]\" width=\"240\" height=\"39\" />\nUsing the rules of modular arithmetic,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05afaa6c153281aca305cbc9929a812a3ee5c4ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2(n+1)^2 \\equiv 68\\pmod {n + 5}\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"19\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cefdc6312981718b8367e81b0af335679b011f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2(n+1)^2 - 68\\equiv 0\\pmod {n + 5}\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"19\" />\nExpanding the left hand side,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed2db2257db47e986bc6eb61b5442d53ca02d132.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^4 + 2 n^3 + n^2 - 68\\equiv 0\\pmod {n + 5}\\]\" width=\"295\" height=\"19\" />\nThis means that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/0154bf3891aef5069f33079f62fead85154b72fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^4 + 2 n^3 + n^2 - 68$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"148\" height=\"16\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/58248972611e626a107f19568252f4b636ce38bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${n + 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e7fcebbe6170dbaec2a7cc4247f21125ed2cf40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n + 5) | (n^4 + 2 n^3 + n^2 - 68)\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"19\" />\nDividing polynomials,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/436bb2e75f4727ec4971bcab2e068cfcaf5c6241.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n^4 + 2 n^3 + n^2 - 68}{n + 5}\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55a96ba06c98b4d4d1329a2fc883eade0ad7d9a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= n^3 - 3 n^2 + 16n - 80 + \\frac{332}{(n + 5)}\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5bde535ba8009d1050a4679cb954f16c155cb65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a131e44938571300020512aceec1fee671ead5ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"7\" height=\"20\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e235c9c4539cc00ba2419cbb23dbf54f24ca5665.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n^4 + 2 n^3 + n^2 - 68)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"19\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b7822aebffad0fc070fac8929eb45da399e369f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\iff$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b887d0d6d09aa018881842769d844c07f47fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{332}{(n + 5)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"58\" height=\"42\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/134004c561e4c0cca193dbf5122e5ca963dd5b7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\in$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d4023589a374e5b4a1bc6063d887aec205e0d3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />\n<br /><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b887d0d6d09aa018881842769d844c07f47fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{332}{(n + 5)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"58\" height=\"42\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/134004c561e4c0cca193dbf5122e5ca963dd5b7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\in$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d4023589a374e5b4a1bc6063d887aec205e0d3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b7822aebffad0fc070fac8929eb45da399e369f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\iff$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d03c3ceb715b523691defee82133e70467148b9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + 5) = \\pm 1, \\pm 2, \\pm 4, \\pm 83, \\pm 166, \\pm 332$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"305\" height=\"18\" />\n<br /><br />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/134004c561e4c0cca193dbf5122e5ca963dd5b7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\in$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e6cd0e4103015efba12e0fc4291f012b467eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/581c3b5d37d20082aefe33310bfef76fd1d332ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 5 &gt; 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> (because the remainder when dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/d/7dd8b1b9017014c56c0f273336fc1b959169e1cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/d/7dd8b1b9017014c56c0f273336fc1b959169e1cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />), so all options <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a70a5507fb5479bd8d8f20d70da5228b6c12ea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> can be eliminated.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/248e2cecb97086f94cfc4c6ef8fee6e44331d3c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n + 5) = 83, 166, 332\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb75f7ae501993f60875f0d2dce01e2e5d410bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = 78, 161, 327\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />\nChecking all 3 cases, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f38dec72a31e27e582eceab61333529c2c4cc3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 78$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96294f38cb4557f55aa7fee142a34ea86b2a018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 161$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> work; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a190a4803aaef1d7f28f787f52bfcfd6c87460b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 327$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> fails.\n<br /><br />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94b957cfe61963a815a2c6cf9adb10239135bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78 + 161 = \\boxed{239}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n<br /><br />\n~ {TSun} ~\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28similar_ideas_to_Solution_1.2C_but_faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(similar_ideas_to_Solution_1,_but_faster)\">Solution 5 (similar ideas to Solution 1, but faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (similar ideas to Solution 1, but faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As before, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86f3d6d0d58da262f3506b941c857fbbf8e534fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5+a)^3 + (n-a)^3 \\equiv (5+a)^3 - (n+5 - (n-a))^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod {n+5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"543\" height=\"19\" />\nThus, we can pair up the terms from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec0dcde3e88efde55a8c8df29fc970f9e6c6da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba37f50c674bcbae995ed1d9dfd4beb5e53c765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> and cancel them. We have to deal with two cases:\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bdfbee249288f74365f9a24b85e374659e86f5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3+6^3 + \\cdots + n^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod {n+5},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"19\" /> as there are an even number of terms and they pair and cancel. We thus get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d0bbb387514c79d3cf17c259993a86ae3c3f224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2+2^3+3^3+4^3 = 100 \\equiv 17 \\pmod {n+5},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"336\" height=\"19\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/140499d536f05c3c4650367839483de67db8ca4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+5) | 83,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbb3bdd8a89a46ad6428ea29a43650c7dae5e817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=78.$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be91c5e23f1d0f7487b739c53bc5300e70b2b303.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^3+2^3+\\cdots + n^3 \\equiv 1^3+2^3+3^3+4^3+\\left( \\frac{n+5}{2} \\right)^3 \\equiv 17 \\pmod {n+5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"549\" height=\"46\" />\nLetting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2e6e464c4290161de4ad99202b5d5f856ce32b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\frac{n+5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d87de9fd958a9edcb1f299544b05c338a0f603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 + 83 \\equiv 0 \\pmod {2k}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" /> However, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c1ad4a48099624f3bbfc16590f9be2d29351d61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$83$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c99a6aaebc17474bd09ea71d84d4e769a0662b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed425403be6323a954cfd72306d137caf7add5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1,83.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />\nPlugging this back into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/f/44f3c4659aeb9a188409e82e0e5910511fd598e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2(83)-5 = 161$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" /> in the latter case.\n</p><p>Thus, the sum of all possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ff91744d9ffb75096b692af9bab0e7c8da53dbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78+161 = \\boxed{239}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>- ccx09\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<pre> There was a link to alcumus instead of a link to a video solution by OmegaLearn here. I tried to search up his video but I couldn't find it. Please find it and insert it here.\n</pre>\n<p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=87Mp0cdUtCU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=87Mp0cdUtCU</a>\n~ North America Math Contest Go Go Go\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/bz5N-jI2e0U?t=201\">https://youtu.be/bz5N-jI2e0U?t=201</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II\" title=\"2020 AIME II\">2020 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\